$CATEGORY: Vocabulary/HansenQuinn/5/prep

::Q001::[markdown]Which preposition + case means “toward (of time)”?:{
	~%-100%ἐν + dat#Incorrect. **ἐν + dat** means “in” (Chapter 1).
	~%100%ὑπὸ + acc#Correct: “toward (of time)” is **ὑπὸ + acc** (Chapter 5).
	~%-100%ἄνευ + gen#Incorrect. **ἄνευ + gen** means “without” (Chapter 7).
	~%-100%ἀντί + gen#Incorrect. **ἀντί + gen** means “instead of” (Chapter 3).
	~%-100%κατά + acc#Incorrect. **κατά + acc** means “down” (Chapter 6).
	~%-100%ὑπὸ + dat#Incorrect. **ὑπὸ + dat** means “under” (Chapter 5).
	~%-100%εἰς + acc#Incorrect. **εἰς + acc** means “into” (Chapter 1).
	~%-100%ὑπὸ + gen#Incorrect. **ὑπὸ + gen** means “by (personal agent)” (Chapter 5).
}


::Q002::[markdown]What does **περί + acc** mean?:{
	~%-100%in front of#Incorrect. **πρό + gen** means “in front of” (Chapter 2).
	~%-100%to the side of#Incorrect. **παρά + acc** means “to the side of” (Chapter 2).
	~%-100%to#Incorrect. **εἰς + acc** means “to” (Chapter 1).
	~%-100%under the power of#Incorrect. **ὑπὸ + dat** means “under the power of” (Chapter 5).
	~%-100%beyond (of motion or measure)#Incorrect. **ὑπέρ + acc** means “beyond (of motion or measure)” (Chapter 9).
	~%100%concerning#Correct: **περί + acc** means “concerning” (Chapter 3).
	~%-100%about#Incorrect. **περί + gen** means “about” (Chapter 3).
	~%-100%according to#Incorrect. **κατά + acc** means “according to” (Chapter 6).
}


::Q003::[markdown]Which preposition + case means “under the power of”?:{
	~%-100%περί + gen#Incorrect. **περί + gen** means “concerning” (Chapter 3).
	~%100%ὑπὸ + dat#Correct: “under the power of” is **ὑπὸ + dat** (Chapter 5).
	~%-100%ὑπὸ + gen#Incorrect. **ὑπὸ + gen** means “by (personal agent)” (Chapter 5).
	~%-100%ὑπὸ + acc#Incorrect. **ὑπὸ + acc** means “under (with motion)” (Chapter 5).
	~%-100%μετά + acc#Incorrect. **μετά + acc** means “after” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%περί + dat#Incorrect. **περί + dat** means “around” (Chapter 3).
	~%-100%περί + acc#Incorrect. **περί + acc** means “around” (Chapter 3).
	~%-100%ἐν + dat#Incorrect. **ἐν + dat** means “in” (Chapter 1).
}


::Q004::[markdown]Which preposition + case means “beside”?:{
	~%-100%παρά + dat#Incorrect. **παρά + dat** means “at the side of” (Chapter 2).
	~%-100%διά + gen#Incorrect. **διά + gen** means “through” (Chapter 3).
	~%100%παρά + acc#Correct: “beside” is **παρά + acc** (Chapter 2).
	~%-100%περί + acc#Incorrect. **περί + acc** means “around” (Chapter 3).
	~%-100%περί + dat#Incorrect. **περί + dat** means “around” (Chapter 3).
	~%-100%εἰς + acc#Incorrect. **εἰς + acc** means “into” (Chapter 1).
	~%-100%διά + acc#Incorrect. **διά + acc** means “on account of” (Chapter 3).
	~%-100%παρά + gen#Incorrect. **παρά + gen** means “from beside” (Chapter 2).
}


